that veterans themselves who i didn't think would&nbsp;
be as into it because they've already lived it um&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:05.920
but how it really became an important film for&nbsp;
a lot of of actual combat vets who felt like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:11.920
watching that they did they're like well if some&nbsp;
filmmaker told the story must not just be me so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:16.720
it helped some of them realize they're not alone&nbsp;
in that struggle that there's others out there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:21.920
that are dealing with same issues you know they&nbsp;
have such a self-reliance that's bred into them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:27.920
through through their military training through&nbsp;
you know their literally i mean their forces of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:32.400
nature when they're in combat and they come&nbsp;
back and they're dealing with these issues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:35.520
and it's almost an embarrassment to admit that&nbsp;
they're dealing with depression that they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:41.440
dealing with social isolation financial issues&nbsp;
all that sort of stuff and so to to showcase it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:46.480
in that way where they can see that this is a&nbsp;
systemic issue it's not a personal flaw theirs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:52.800
that it's something that's happening to a lot&nbsp;
of people it's great to see that response to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.800 --> 00:13:00.400
it as well um obviously it was something that was&nbsp;
personally really important to me uh it was also&nbsp;&nbsp;

